config BR2_PACKAGE_GL4ES
	bool "gl4es"
	depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS
	help
	  gl4es implements desktop OpenGL 1.5 (and much of 2.1) on top
	  of OpenGL ES 1.1/2.0, so legacy GL games and apps run on
	  GPUs whose drivers only expose GLES - Mali, older Adreno and
	  friends.

	  It installs to /usr/lib/gl4es so it never shadows a real
	  libGL: programs opt in with
	  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/gl4es.

	  https://github.com/ptitSeb/gl4es

comment "gl4es needs a toolchain with dynamic libraries"
	depends on BR2_STATIC_LIBS
